{"title":"Career Roadmap — Game Designer","role":"Game Designer","summary":"A Game Designer creates the rules, systems, mechanics, challenges, progression, player interactions, and overall gameplay experience of a game.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Film & Video Communication"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Game Designer creates the rules, systems, mechanics, challenges, progression, player interactions, and overall gameplay experience of a game."},{"type":"p","text":"A Game Designer is different from a Game Artist or Game Programmer:"},{"type":"note","label":"Game Designer","text":"Decides how the game works and feels to play"},{"type":"note","label":"Game Artist","text":"Creates how the game looks"},{"type":"note","label":"Game Programmer","text":"Builds how the game functions technically"},{"type":"note","label":"Level Designer","text":"Designs specific playable spaces, encounters and levels"},{"type":"note","label":"Game Producer","text":"Coordinates people, schedule, budget and delivery"},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Des student, Game Design is particularly suitable for students who combine creative thinking + storytelling + systems thinking + user psychology + basic technology."}]},{"heading":"What a Game Designer Does","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developing game concepts"},{"text":"Defining game rules and objectives"},{"text":"Designing gameplay mechanics"},{"text":"Creating player progression systems"},{"text":"Designing challenges and rewards"},{"text":"Creating game loops"},{"text":"Designing levels and encounters"},{"text":"Developing game narratives with writers"},{"text":"Creating prototypes"},{"text":"Playtesting games"},{"text":"Analysing player behaviour"},{"text":"Balancing difficulty and progression"},{"text":"Working with artists and programmers"},{"text":"Preparing Game Design Documents (GDDs)"},{"text":"Iterating based on player feedback"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A professional Game Designer spends significant time testing, analysing and refining ideas, not just brainstorming game concepts."}]},{"heading":"Core Knowledge Required","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"A. Game Design Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Game dynamics"},{"text":"Player goals"},{"text":"Rules"},{"text":"Feedback systems"},{"text":"Reward systems"},{"text":"Challenge"},{"text":"Risk/reward"},{"text":"Game loops"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Difficulty curves"},{"text":"Player motivation"},{"text":"Game economy"},{"text":"Replayability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"B. Game Genres"},{"type":"p","text":"Study the design principles behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Action"},{"text":"Adventure"},{"text":"RPG"},{"text":"Strategy"},{"text":"Simulation"},{"text":"Sports"},{"text":"Racing"},{"text":"Puzzle"},{"text":"Platformer"},{"text":"Survival"},{"text":"Horror"},{"text":"Multiplayer"},{"text":"Mobile games"},{"text":"Casual games"},{"text":"Educational games"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is not to master every genre but to understand how design decisions differ between them."}]},{"heading":"Game Design Fundamentals to Master","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong student should be able to explain:"},{"type":"h","text":"Core Game Loop"},{"type":"flow","items":["Player Action","Game Response","Reward / Feedback","New Challenge","Player Decision","Repeat"]},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Explore","Fight","Collect","Upgrade","Explore"]},{"type":"p","text":"The quality of this loop strongly influences whether a game remains engaging."}]},{"heading":"Important Game Design Concepts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Rules, interactions, actions"}],[{"text":"Gameplay"},{"text":"Player experience and interaction"}],[{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Levels, upgrades, unlocks"}],[{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Challenge balancing"}],[{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Currency, resources, rewards"}],[{"text":"Narrative"},{"text":"Story, characters, world-building"}],[{"text":"Level Design"},{"text":"Spaces, encounters, pacing"}],[{"text":"UX"},{"text":"Menus, controls, feedback"}],[{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Motivation, engagement"}],[{"text":"Multiplayer"},{"text":"Competition, cooperation"}],[{"text":"Monetisation"},{"text":"F2P, premium, DLC, cosmetic systems"}],[{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Inclusive controls and experiences"}],[{"text":"Analytics"},{"text":"Player behaviour and retention"}]]}]},{"heading":"Software & Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should gain practical experience with at least one major game engine."},{"type":"h","text":"Game Engines"},{"type":"h","text":"Unity"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"C#"},{"text":"2D/3D development"},{"text":"Mobile games"},{"text":"Indie games"},{"text":"Prototyping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Unreal Engine"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blueprints"},{"text":"C++"},{"text":"3D games"},{"text":"AAA workflows"},{"text":"Cinematic/virtual production"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Other tools may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Godot"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"Maya"},{"text":"3ds Max"},{"text":"Substance 3D"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Perforce"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student does not need to master every tool."},{"type":"p","text":"A practical combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Unreal/Unity","basic programming","Blender","Git","design documentation"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Programming Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Game Designer does not necessarily need to become a full-time programmer."},{"type":"p","text":"However, programming knowledge is highly valuable."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended"},{"type":"p","text":"For Unity:"},{"type":"h","text":"C#"},{"type":"p","text":"For Unreal:"},{"type":"h","text":"Blueprints + basic C++"},{"type":"p","text":"Important concepts:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Conditions"},{"text":"Loops"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Object-oriented programming"},{"text":"State machines"},{"text":"Input systems"},{"text":"Basic debugging"},{"text":"Game logic"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal profile"},{"type":"p","text":"Game Design"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Basic Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Game Engine"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Level Design"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Player Psychology"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination makes the graduate more versatile."}]},{"heading":"Game Design Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"One of the most important professional skills is writing a Game Design Document (GDD)."},{"type":"p","text":"A GDD may contain:"},{"type":"h","text":"Game Concept"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game title"},{"text":"Genre"},{"text":"Platform"},{"text":"Target audience"},{"text":"Core experience"},{"text":"Unique selling point"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Core loop"},{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Controls"},{"text":"Objectives"},{"text":"Challenges"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Progression"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Levels"},{"text":"XP"},{"text":"Unlocks"},{"text":"Skills"},{"text":"Rewards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"World"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"Characters"},{"text":"Story"},{"text":"Lore"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical Requirements"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engine"},{"text":"Platform"},{"text":"Multiplayer requirements"},{"text":"Performance considerations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A student should create GDDs for their portfolio rather than simply writing game ideas."}]},{"heading":"B.Des Academic Roadmap","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drawing"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Design thinking"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Typography"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Creative problem solving"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Alongside this, begin:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game analysis"},{"text":"Basic Unity/Unreal"},{"text":"Basic programming"},{"text":"Simple game prototypes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target"},{"type":"p","text":"Create 2–3 small playable prototypes."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Game Design Specialisation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Game loops"},{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Narrative design"},{"text":"Game UX"},{"text":"Character design fundamentals"},{"text":"Game art pipelines"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Playtesting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unity or Unreal"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"Git"},{"text":"Basic scripting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"2D game"},{"text":"3D prototype"},{"text":"Level prototype"},{"text":"Game Design Document"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Professional Game Development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced gameplay systems"},{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Game balancing"},{"text":"Game economies"},{"text":"Multiplayer concepts"},{"text":"Player analytics"},{"text":"UX"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Production workflows"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Start working in teams:"},{"type":"p","text":"Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Programmer"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Artist"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Animator"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Sound Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"The ability to collaborate is critical because commercial games are team-based products."}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Industry Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus heavily on portfolio development."},{"type":"p","text":"Build at least:"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Complete Small Game"},{"type":"p","text":"A polished playable game rather than a huge unfinished project."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Gameplay Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate a strong mechanic."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Level Design Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Concept"},{"text":"Blockout"},{"text":"Gameplay flow"},{"text":"Enemy placement"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Playtesting"},{"text":"Final version"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Systems Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"RPG character progression system"},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XP system"},{"text":"Skill tree"},{"text":"Currency"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Balancing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Experimental Game"},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted game"},{"text":"Educational game"},{"text":"VR game"},{"text":"Narrative game"},{"text":"Social/multiplayer prototype"}]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Structure","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Game Designer's portfolio should demonstrate thinking + implementation, not only attractive screenshots."},{"type":"p","text":"For every project show:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem / Concept","Design Goal","Research","Game Mechanics","Prototype","Playtesting","Problems Identified","Iteration","Final Result","What I Learned"]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong portfolio evidence"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Playable builds"},{"text":"Short gameplay videos"},{"text":"GDD extracts"},{"text":"Level maps"},{"text":"Flow diagrams"},{"text":"Wireframes"},{"text":"Mechanics prototypes"},{"text":"Playtesting results"},{"text":"Iteration examples"},{"text":"Design decisions"}]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Recommended projects:"},{"type":"table","header":["Project","Skills Demonstrated"],"rows":[[{"text":"2D Platformer"},{"text":"Mechanics"}],[{"text":"Puzzle Game"},{"text":"Systems Design"}],[{"text":"RPG Prototype"},{"text":"Progression"}],[{"text":"Multiplayer Prototype"},{"text":"Systems"}],[{"text":"Horror Level"},{"text":"Pacing"}],[{"text":"Mobile Game"},{"text":"UX"}],[{"text":"Educational Game"},{"text":"Serious Games"}],[{"text":"VR Prototype"},{"text":"Immersive Design"}],[{"text":"AI Game Prototype"},{"text":"Emerging Technology"}],[{"text":"Level Redesign"},{"text":"Analytical Design"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A small polished game is generally more valuable than a large unfinished game."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students should seek internships from the second year onward."},{"type":"h","text":"Suitable internship roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game Design Intern"},{"text":"Level Design Intern"},{"text":"Game QA Intern"},{"text":"Game UX Intern"},{"text":"Narrative Design Intern"},{"text":"Game Production Intern"},{"text":"Game Research Intern"},{"text":"Technical Game Design Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Where to gain experience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game studios"},{"text":"Indie studios"},{"text":"Mobile game companies"},{"text":"VR/AR companies"},{"text":"Educational technology companies"},{"text":"Simulation companies"},{"text":"Serious-game companies"},{"text":"Interactive media studios"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Indie projects and student game-development teams can also provide useful portfolio experience."}]},{"heading":"Game Jams","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Game jams are especially valuable."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Global Game Jam"},{"text":"Ludum Dare"},{"text":"GMTK Game Jam"},{"text":"itch.io game jams"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should aim to experience:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Idea","Design","Prototype","Development","Testing","Submission"]},{"type":"p","text":"within a short timeframe."},{"type":"p","text":"This teaches rapid iteration and teamwork."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certifications are supplementary."},{"type":"p","text":"More important:"},{"type":"h","text":"Playable portfolio > certificate collection"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas for structured learning include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unity development"},{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Game design"},{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"3D modelling"},{"text":"C#/C++"},{"text":"Game UX"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"Interactive storytelling"},{"text":"Game production"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Engine-specific credentials can be useful when they correspond to actual practical capability, but employers generally assess portfolio quality and demonstrated skills heavily."}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After developing general Game Design skills, the student can specialise."},{"type":"h","text":"1. Gameplay Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Combat"},{"text":"Controls"},{"text":"Player abilities"},{"text":"Game systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Level Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maps"},{"text":"Encounters"},{"text":"Pacing"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Player navigation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Systems Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Skills"},{"text":"Resources"},{"text":"Game balance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Narrative Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Characters"},{"text":"World-building"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Technical Game Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Combines:"},{"type":"p","text":"Design + Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"This is a particularly strong technical route."},{"type":"h","text":"6. Game UX Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interfaces"},{"text":"Controls"},{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Player onboarding"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"7. Multiplayer Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Competitive systems"},{"text":"Cooperation"},{"text":"Matchmaking concepts"},{"text":"Game balance"},{"text":"Social mechanics"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Game Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI is becoming increasingly relevant to game development."},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI should be treated as a design and production tool, not a replacement for design judgement."},{"type":"h","text":"Areas where AI can assist"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NPC behaviour"},{"text":"Procedural content"},{"text":"Dialogue prototyping"},{"text":"Concept exploration"},{"text":"Texture generation"},{"text":"Animation assistance"},{"text":"Game testing"},{"text":"Player behaviour analysis"},{"text":"Difficulty adaptation"},{"text":"Voice prototyping"},{"text":"World generation"},{"text":"Rapid prototyping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Game Designer","AI-assisted ideation","Prototype","Player Testing","Analytics","Human Design Decisions","Iteration"]},{"type":"p","text":"Human judgement remains important for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game feel"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Narrative quality"},{"text":"Player experience"},{"text":"Creative direction"}]}]},{"heading":"Emerging Areas","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should watch developments in:"},{"type":"h","text":"AI Games"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI NPCs"},{"text":"Adaptive narratives"},{"text":"Generative environments"},{"text":"Intelligent game testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"XR"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"VR"},{"text":"AR"},{"text":"Mixed Reality"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud Gaming"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Streaming games"},{"text":"Cross-platform experiences"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Serious Games"},{"type":"p","text":"Games for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Training"},{"text":"Defence"},{"text":"Simulation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"UGC Games"},{"type":"p","text":"User-generated content platforms are creating new opportunities for designers to build experiences and systems rather than only traditional standalone games."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After B.Des, suitable postgraduate routes include:"},{"type":"h","text":"M.Des"},{"type":"p","text":"Specialisations may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game Design"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"UX Design"},{"text":"Animation"},{"text":"Digital Media"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Game Design"},{"text":"MSc Game Technology"},{"text":"MA Interactive Media"},{"text":"Master's in Animation"},{"text":"Master's in Digital Arts"},{"text":"Master's in XR/Immersive Media"},{"text":"Game Technology programmes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The right choice depends on whether the student wants to become more design-oriented, technical, artistic, or research-oriented."}]},{"heading":"Higher Education Direction","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a student targeting top-level game design roles, higher education can be useful when it provides:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong game-development labs"},{"text":"Industry projects"},{"text":"Experienced faculty"},{"text":"Professional game studios nearby"},{"text":"Game-jam ecosystem"},{"text":"Strong alumni network"},{"text":"Portfolio development"},{"text":"Research opportunities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential international destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"France"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Japan"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Programme accreditation, portfolio requirements, costs and qualification recognition should be checked against current university and country rules before applying."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A typical progression could be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Game Design Intern","Junior Game Designer","Game Designer","Mid-Level Game Designer","Senior Game Designer","Lead Game Designer","Principal / Lead Designer","Game Director / Creative Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative progression:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Game Designer","Systems Designer","Senior Systems Designer","Lead Systems Designer"]},{"type":"p","text":"or:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Game Designer","Technical Game Designer","Senior Technical Designer","Technical Design Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Related Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The same degree can lead to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game Designer"},{"text":"Gameplay Designer"},{"text":"Systems Designer"},{"text":"Level Designer"},{"text":"Technical Game Designer"},{"text":"Narrative Designer"},{"text":"Game UX Designer"},{"text":"Game Economy Designer"},{"text":"Game Producer"},{"text":"Game Researcher"},{"text":"Serious Games Designer"},{"text":"VR/AR Experience Designer"},{"text":"Interactive Experience Designer"},{"text":"Game QA Analyst"},{"text":"Game Design Consultant"}]}]},{"heading":"Skill-Gap Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Beginner","Job Ready","Advanced"],"rows":[[{"text":"Game Mechanics"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Expert"}],[{"text":"Game Engine"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Level Design"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Game Balancing"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Narrative"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Game UX"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Playtesting"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Analytics"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Team Collaboration"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"h","text":"Game Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Game loops"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Balancing"},{"text":"Player psychology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"h","text":"Unity or Unreal\nC# / Blueprints\nGit\nBasic 3D tools"},{"type":"h","text":"Creative"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Visual thinking"},{"text":"World-building"},{"text":"Concept development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GDD writing"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Team collaboration"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Playtesting"},{"text":"Project management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted development"},{"text":"Procedural generation"},{"text":"XR"},{"text":"Player analytics"}]}]},{"heading":"What Students Should Avoid","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"❌ Only learning software"},{"type":"p","text":"Knowing Unity or Unreal does not automatically make someone a Game Designer."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Only making concept art"},{"type":"p","text":"Game Design requires playable systems and interaction."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Creating huge projects"},{"type":"p","text":"A 20-minute polished game is often better portfolio evidence than a 3-year unfinished RPG."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Ignoring programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Even basic scripting significantly improves a designer's ability to prototype."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Ignoring playtesting"},{"type":"p","text":"A game that looks good can still be poorly designed."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Collecting certificates without projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Recruitment in creative/game roles is strongly portfolio-oriented."}]},{"heading":"Ideal 4-Year Development Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Primary Goal","Portfolio Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design foundations"},{"text":"2–3 prototypes"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Game design skills"},{"text":"3–4 playable projects"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Team game + advanced system"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Industry readiness"},{"text":"4–6 polished portfolio projects"}]]}]},{"heading":"Placement Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unity/Unreal"},{"text":"Basic programming"},{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Game balancing"},{"text":"Game UX"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GDD"},{"text":"Game analysis"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Playtesting"},{"text":"Player psychology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Interview Preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"Be prepared to answer:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why does a particular game mechanic work?"},{"text":"How would you redesign an existing game?"},{"text":"How would you balance a weapon?"},{"text":"How would you design a tutorial?"},{"text":"How would you increase player engagement without making the game unfair?"},{"text":"How would you design a level for beginners?"},{"text":"How would you identify why players are leaving a game?"},{"text":"How would you design a progression system?"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A candidate should be able to defend design decisions with reasoning, not simply say that something “looks good.”"}]},{"heading":"Best Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an ideal candidate should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Des in Game Design / Games Art"},{"text":"Strong understanding of game mechanics"}]},{"type":"note","label":"One primary engine","text":"Unity or Unreal"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic programming ability"},{"text":"Level-design experience"},{"text":"Systems-design knowledge"},{"text":"Game UX understanding"},{"text":"GDD writing ability"},{"text":"Game-jam experience"},{"text":"1–2 internships or equivalent industry/team experience"},{"text":"4–6 polished portfolio projects"},{"text":"At least 2 genuinely playable games"},{"text":"One strong systems-design project"},{"text":"One strong level-design project"},{"text":"Git/GitHub familiarity"},{"text":"Playtesting experience"},{"text":"Professional portfolio website"},{"text":"Gameplay videos/showreel"},{"text":"Understanding of AI-assisted game development"},{"text":"Ability to work with programmers, artists, writers and producers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strongest Graduate Profile"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Game Design","Unity/Unreal","Basic Programming","Level Design","Systems Design","Playtesting","4–6 Playable Projects","Game Jams","Internship"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination gives the graduate multiple entry points into the game industry rather than restricting them to a single job title."}]}]}